From: virtudude <virtudude@protonmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] input: qcom-hv-haptics: stop zero-amplitude effects immediately

A zero-amplitude update while playing dropped gain to 1 and deferred
the stop by 5 s. The stop applies the configured brake pattern, so
rumble ended with a distinct tap 5 s after the game stopped it.

Erase the active effect immediately instead, and ignore a following
playback request when no effect is loaded so it cannot restart stale
motor state.

Ported from Armada: https://github.com/armada-os/armada/blob/410bcf26a67f3e5d38e487d0ec84c5632f2bc3f6/packages/kernel/patches/1004-input-haptics-stop-zero-amplitude-immediately.patch
---
--- a/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
+++ b/drivers/input/misc/qcom-hv-haptics.c
@@ -2699,6 +2699,8 @@ static void haptics_stop_constant_effect_play(struct work_struct *work)
 		dev_err(chip->dev, "disable hpwr_vreg failed\n");
 }
 
+static int haptics_erase(struct input_dev *dev, int effect_id);
+
 static int haptics_upload_effect(struct input_dev *dev,
 		struct ff_effect *effect, struct ff_effect *old);
 
@@ -2740,16 +2742,7 @@ static int haptics_upload_effect(struct input_dev *dev,
 		pr_debug("tried to upload an effect while the chip was busy playing, setting gain...\n");
 
 		if (gain == 0) {
-			//The purpose of scheduling a stop_work work is that if the program calls playback afterwards, it will play
-			// for a very short time using the previous gain
-			// ( Like Aethersx2, it likes to call playback with zero value EVEN when amplitude is zero)
-			//We cant stop the playback now, so schedule rumble stop after 5s
-			//and set the gain to a low value (essentially zero)
-
-			dev_dbg(chip->dev, "scheduling stop after 500ms, because gain is zero\n");
-
-			dev->ff->set_gain(dev, 1);
-			schedule_delayed_work(&chip->stop_work, msecs_to_jiffies(5000));
+			return haptics_erase(dev, effect->id);
 		} else {
 			dev_dbg(chip->dev, "Setting gain to %hu...\n", gain);
 
@@ -2859,8 +2852,10 @@ static int haptics_playback(struct input_dev *dev, int effect_id, int val)
 	dev_dbg(chip->dev, "playback val = %d\n", val);
 
 	if (!!val && !chip->chip_is_playing) {
-		if (!chip->chip_effect_loaded)
-			dev_warn(chip->dev, "Trying to playback while no effect is loaded!\n");
+		if (!chip->chip_effect_loaded) {
+			dev_dbg(chip->dev, "Trying to playback while no effect is loaded!\n");
+			return 0;
+		}
 
 		return haptics_enable_play(chip, true);
 	}
